Java version of the shell from there we can create variables
Assume we want to create a variable and then autocomplete it we press tab, after pressing the first letter
but if there are multiple variables with the same name the jshell will suggest us possible completions.
/vars - check all variables assigned thus far

You can define everything in the jshell, classes and methods.
we create the following method:
jshell> int factorial(int n){
   ...>     if (n <=1)
jshell> int factorial(int n){
   ...>     if (n <=1)e all possible completions; total possible completions: 1,414>
   ...>     return n;
   ...>     return n*factorial(n-1);
